      "items": [
        {
          "label": {
            "zh": "已知卫星",
            "en": "Known Moons"
          },
          "value": {
            "zh": "木卫二是木星的卫星，本身无已知天然卫星",
            "en": "Europa is a moon of Jupiter; it has no known natural satellites"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "zh": "卫星名称",
            "en": "Moon Names"
          },
          "value": {
            "zh": "木卫二（Europa）是木星第四大卫星",
            "en": "Europa is Jupiter's fourth-largest moon"
          }
        }
      ],
      "note": {
        "zh": "※ 木卫二是伽利略卫星中最小的一个，但因其冰下海洋成为太阳系中最有希望找到地外生命的地点之一。",
        "en": "※ Europa is the smallest of the Galilean moons, yet its subsurface ocean makes it one of the most promising places to search for extraterrestrial life in the Solar System."
      }
    },
    {
      "title": {
        "zh": "🌋 地表特征",
        "en": "🌋 Surface Features"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "label": {
            "zh": "主要地形",
            "en": "Main Terrain"
          },
          "value": {
            "zh": "冰壳平原、暗色裂隙带（线纹）、混沌地形、冰丘",
            "en": "Ice plains, dark fracture bands (lineae), chaotic terrain, ice domes"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "zh": "最大撞击坑",
            "en": "Largest Crater"
          },
          "value": {
            "zh": "普尔瓦（Pwyll）撞击坑，直径约 26 公里",
            "en": "Pwyll crater, ~26 km diameter"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "zh": "地表年龄",
            "en": "Surface Age"
          },
          "value": {
            "zh": "约 2000 万至 1.8 亿年（非常年轻）",
            "en": "~20 million to 180 million years (very young)"
          }
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "zh": "最高峰",
            "en": "Highest Peak"
          },
          "value": {
            "zh": "无明显高山，地形起伏一般不超过数百米",
            "en": "No prominent mountains; relief generally < a few hundred meters"
          }
        }
      ],
      "note": {
        "zh": "※ 木卫二表面布满纵横交错的暗色裂隙，称为“线纹”，有些长达数千公里，是冰壳因潮汐应力反复开裂和重新冻结形成的。",
        "en": "※ Europa's surface is crisscrossed by dark fractures called 'lineae', some thousands of kilometers long, formed by repeated cracking and refreezing of the ice shell due to tidal stresses."
      }
    },
